 gray:"A 60-year-old heavy smoking obese man presented with chest tightness for a week. Last night he climbed a flight of stairs. He felt tired and couldn't lie down. BP 160/90, no edema, no orthopnea. no murmur, no LVH, no heaving Lab Cr 1.1, high sensitivity troponin T not elevated EKG : generalized ST depression? What is the diagnosis? — 1. Aortic dissection 2. Pericarditis 3. STEMI 4. NSTEMI 5. Unstable angina",
